# Repository layout

- **`app/`** — App Router pages, route groups (e.g. `(auth)`, `(dashboard)`), `layout.tsx`, `providers.tsx`, `globals.css`, and **`app/api/**`** Route Handlers (BFF).
- **`components/`** — `ui/*` shared primitives; feature folders per product area.
- **`lib/`** — `auth.ts`, `auth-fetch.ts`, `bff.ts`, `bff-logging.ts`, `constants.ts`, `env.ts`, `i18n.ts`, `jwt.ts`, `logging.ts`, `upstream-fetch.ts`, `utils.ts`.

## BFF route organization

Organize **`app/api/**`** by **upstream service module name**, not by UI feature.

### Correct

```text
app/api/
├── auth/                    # Portal session (this app)
└── <upstream-service>/      # One folder per upstream microservice
    └── <resource>/
        └── route.ts
```

Use the **canonical upstream service name** from `product/00-service-profile.md` and `product/02-route-map.md`.

### Wrong

```text
app/api/
├── tenants/       # Ambiguous — which upstream owns this?
├── devices/
└── users/
```

**Rationale:** Clear ownership, service-specific error handling, aligns with backend team boundaries.

## UI route organization

Organize **`app/(dashboard)/**`** by **user workflows**, not by upstream service.

```text
app/(dashboard)/
├── platform/           # Platform-wide operations
├── organizations/      # Cross-tenant admin flows
└── organization/       # Single-tenant context
```

## Conventions

- **New BFF route:** `app/api/<upstream-service>/<resource>/route.ts`
- **New UI screen:** under `app/` in the appropriate route group
- **Do not** add a separate backend in this repo — one Next.js application

## Configuration

- **Static config** (`.env`): upstream base URLs, cookie names, log levels
- **Dynamic config** (API): tenant settings, feature flags — prefer API over env for business variation

Portal UX patterns: `docs/project-guidance/` (see `documentation-project-guidance.mdc`).
